WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.780
FedRAMP Moderate has direct engineering implications.

2
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:23.480
It influences secure configuration, identity and access management, least privilege, audit logging, encryption, vulnerability management, change control, incident response readiness, backup and recovery, monitoring, secure development practices, and infrastructure automation.

3
00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.780
These are not abstract compliance topics.

4
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:32.000
They are design and operations choices that affect how the system behaves every day.

5
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:37.080
A Moderate-oriented service should be evidence-producing by design.

6
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:40.940
If access is reviewed, the system should preserve review records.

7
00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:46.400
If infrastructure is deployed through code, change history and approval workflows should be available.

8
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:52.820
If vulnerabilities are scanned and remediated, tickets and scan outputs should tell a coherent story.

9
00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:57.720
If incidents are triaged, response records should show decisions and actions.

10
00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:01.900
Evidence should come from normal work rather than emergency reconstruction.

11
00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:07.860
Configuration baselines and infrastructure-as-code can make Moderate operations more repeatable.

12
00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:14.280
They help teams reduce drift, review changes, enforce secure defaults, and prove how environments are built.

13
00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:21.660
Logging and monitoring should be designed early so security-relevant events are captured, retained, protected, and reviewed.

14
00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:30.480
Identity design should support least privilege, administrative accountability, and separation of duties without relying on informal trust.

15
00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:34.040
Engineering teams also need to think about maintainability.

16
00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:38.940
A control that only works when one person remembers a manual step is fragile.

17
00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:48.080
A control that is built into deployment workflows, monitoring routines, ticketing processes, and operational dashboards is easier to sustain.

18
00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:53.940
Moderate success depends on systems that can be operated consistently, not only described well.

19
00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:58.440
The stronger the operational design, the stronger the assessment story becomes.
